{
  "_id": "tg-son",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Sarah … shall bear thee a son, Gen. 17:19 (18:10; Rom. 9:9). son of this bondwoman shall not be heir, Gen. 21:10 (Gal. 4:30). Take now thy son, thine only son Isaac, Gen. 22:2. if it be a son, then ye shall kill him, Ex. 1:16. woman conceived, and bare a son, Ex. 2:2. he became her son … Moses, Ex. 2:10. Thus saith the Lord, Israel is my son, Ex. 4:22. If a man die, and have no son, Num. 27:8. teach them thy sons, and thy sons’ sons, Deut. 4:9. thou shalt say unto thy son, Deut. 6:21. If a man have a stubborn and rebellious son, Deut. 21:18. she bare a son … Samuel, 1 Sam. 1:20. O Absalom, my son, 2 Sam. 18:33 (19:4). son of the woman … fell sick, 1 Kgs. 17:17. he … made his son to pass through the fire, 2 Kgs. 16:3. trust in thee before the sons of men, Ps. 31:19. he beholdeth all the sons of men, Ps. 33:13. they sacrificed their sons … unto devils, Ps. 106:37. wise son maketh a glad father, Prov. 10:1 (15:20). He that spareth his rod hateth his son, Prov. 13:24. foolish son is a grief to his father, Prov. 17:25. Chasten thy son while there is hope, Prov. 19:18. Correct thy son, and he shall give thee rest, Prov. 29:17. heart of the sons of men is full of evil, Eccl. 9:3. How art thou fallen … Lucifer, son of the morning, Isa. 14:12 (D&C 76:26). bring my sons from far, Isa. 43:6. they shall bring thy sons in their arms, Isa. 49:22 (1 Ne. 21:22; 2 Ne. 6:6). thy sons shall come from far, Isa. 60:4. son shall not bear the iniquity of the father, Ezek. 18:20. Ye are the sons of the living God, Hosea 1:10. called my son out of Egypt, Hosea 11:1 (Matt. 2:15). your sons and your daughters shall prophesy, Joel 2:28 (Acts 2:17). neither was I a prophet’s son, Amos 7:14. the son dishonoureth the father, Micah 7:6. he shall purify the sons of Levi, Mal. 3:3.",
